	doi = {10.1109/IWCMC69287.2026.11579996},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105044691531?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {The rapid development in civilian use of drones brings the focus on safety and security problems, particularly with respect to public space and airspace applications, demanding reliable detection in real time. Thus, as a remedy to these challenges, it has been identified that Edge AI comes as an attractive paradigm which facilitates resource-efficient and low-latency inference from data sources. To address these issues, we propose an Edge AI-Based High-Accuracy, Lightweight, Enhanced YOLOv11 (EHALEYO) for real-time small unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) detection in complex environments. EHALEYO incorporates depthwise convolution and integrates RepViT with Efficient Channel Attention (ECA) for enhanced feature extraction to increase feature representation and detection accuracy. Moreover, EHALEYO employed a lightweight LSDECD detection head to maintain the size of the model while preserving accuracy. Experimental evaluations demonstrate the efficiency of the proposed EHALEYO compared to existing methods. It reduces the model size by 41.5-62.1%, computational complexity by 33.9-53.6%, and storage footprint by 38.1-54.4% on the DUT dataset. Furthermore, EHALEYO outperforms all competing approaches on the VisDrone dataset, achieving superior performance with only 3.9 GFLOPs and 1.03M parameters. EHALEYO outperforms YOLOv11n on Raspberry Pi 5, achieving 43.5% higher FPS, 30.3% lower per-frame latency, and 30.2% lower energy consumption per inference, allowing for effective real-time edge deployment. © 2026 IEEE.},
