	abstract = {In recent years, the increasing number of Sudden Unintended Acceleration (SUA) incidents has underscored the need for reliable, real-time verification methods in vehicles. This paper proposes an efficient method for real-time edge AI inference to verify SUA events. To achieve this, we present an Edge AI framework that integrates sensor-derived pedal displacement data with visual evidence of driver pedal operations, deploying light-weight convolutional neural networks (CNNs) on Jetson-based edge devices. Unlike cloud-dependent systems, the proposed approach provides robust and low-latency inference under resource-constrained environments. Furthermore, class-granularity optimization is applied to balance recognition performance with clear decision boundaries, enhancing model stability in complex classification tasks. Experimental results show that the proposed framework achieves high accuracy with low latency, demonstrating its practicality as a consumer-oriented verification tool for SUA. This study contributes not only a technical Edge AI solution but also a societal perspective on accident liability and automotive safety. © 2026 IEEE.},
