	abstract = {The proposed work presents a practical onboard method to identify safe landing zones for Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) during low battery voltage and remote control signal loss fail-safe conditions. In the proposed work, a custom dataset was created through collection of footage at various altitudes ranging between 8-15 m. On the created custom dataset, a deep learning-based object detection algorithm with real-time vision-guided landing control was trained and deployed on an edge device. A lightweight YOLOv8n-based object detection model was custom-trained and optimized using post-training int8 quantization for deployment on Raspberry Pi 4. The controlled autonomous descent was enabled by centroid-based alignment and the model was validated through, both ROS-Gazebo simulation and real-world flight tests. It was observed that post-training quantization reduced model size by 44.6% while maintaining 93.6% mAP. The quantized model achieved an average model inference latency of 42 ms per frame, resulting in an end-to-end processing rate of approximately 14 fps on Raspberry Pi 4, enabling real-time onboard operation under resource constraints. © 2026 IEEE.},
