	abstract = {Autonomous vehicles (AVs) have the potential to significantly enhance the existing transportation system by increasing operational efficiency and reducing the frequency of accidents. However, AVs pose a significant safety concern, particularly in rare and complex real-world scenarios. To address this concern, we propose an integrated framework that combines wireless edge intelligence, reinforcement learning (RL), and generative AI (GenAI) to make AVs adaptive for real-time decision-making for sudden event detection, navigation, path planning, etc. The proposed framework utilizes RL algorithms to allow AVs to learn from experience and adjust their actions in challenging situations. To improve decision-making, GenAI modules are incorporated, including conditional generative adversarial networks (cGANs) for generating synthetic data. The NVIDIA Jetson Xavier is utilized for on-device data processing, analysis, and robust path optimization, ensuring performance in unusual and varied driving conditions that are difficult for traditional approaches. The NVIDIA Jetson Xavier is utilized for on-device data processing, analysis, and robust path optimization, ensuring low-latency responses for critical safety decisions. Extensive simulations of diverse experiments and validations with real-time hardware demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed framework in handling rare situations, such as the sudden presence of obstacles and unpredictable vehicle behavior. The results demonstrate accurate trajectory prediction, accident avoidance, and policy generalization. The proposed framework with RL and GenAI ensures a strong foundation for adaptable, safer, reliable, and more robust AV systems. © 2026 Published by Elsevier B.V.},
