	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105043983983?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Real-time video analytics is a key enabling technology for smart security and industrial Internet of Things (IoT) scenarios. For edge deployment, existing solutions still face three key bottlenecks: poor robustness from cross-framework model conversion, high Central Processing Unit (CPU)-side postprocessing latency, and lack of semantic interaction capability. This paper proposes an efficient video analytics and semantic retrieval system for edge heterogeneous Neural Processing Unit (NPU) platforms. We design three core modules: a Hierarchical Adaptive Tensor Alignment (HATA) algorithm, a hardwareaware end-to-end inference optimization scheme, and a Large Language Model (LLM)-based multi-agent cognitive interaction layer. Experimental results show the system stabilizes postprocessing latency below 3 ms, achieves 45.01 ms end-to-end latency on RK3588, and supports natural language semantic retrieval, meeting industrial edge deployment requirements. © 2026 IEEE.},
