	doi = {10.1109/ICECI69159.2026.11519423},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105041502687?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {The significant growth in complex and latency-sensitive applications across IoT, vehicular networks, and UAV-assisted environments has raised the importance of Mobile Edge Computing (MEC). Task offloading plays an essential enabler in reducing the burden on devices with limited resources by efficiently utilizing edge server network infrastructures. However, to make optimal offloading decisions requires sophisticated optimization methods due to the inherent complexity of resource allocation, task dependencies, mobility, and latency constraints. This survey presents a comprehensive review of recent advancements in optimization techniques for task offloading also classify approaches into heuristic, metaheuristic, deep reinforcement learning, and hybrid models, highlighting methodologies such as Deep QLearning, Whale Optimization, Genetic Algorithms, Lyapunov optimization, and multi-agent systems. A variety of applications are covered under the analysis, which include geo-distributed edge architectures, multi-UAV systems, and vehicle networks. This paper identifies current research gaps, discusses emerging trends, and proposes future research directions toward achieving scalable, adaptive, and real-time offloading strategies. © 2026 IEEE.},
