	abstract = {The increase in parking demand resulting from swift urbanization has intensified congestion in parking facilities, leading to time loss, energy expenditure, and heightened pollution emissions. Conventional parking systems utilizing sensors or manual oversight lack the real-time responsiveness and scalability necessary for smart city applications. This study proposes an Edge-Enabled Smart Parking Management System utilizing deep learning for image identification, integrated with the YOLOv3 car detection algorithm to address these constraints. The system employs an edge-computing architecture, wherein high-quality parking-lot video streams are analyzed on-site using embedded devices (e.g., NVIDIA Jetson Xavier NX). This can diminish dependence on cloud infrastructure, minimize latency, and enhance data privacy. The YOLOv9 network, with the GiraffeDet backbone and Programmable Gradient Information (PGI) module, demonstrates superiority in resilient vehicle recognition over diverse illumination, obstructions, and weather situations. The model was trained on an integrated dataset comprising PKLot, UA-DETRAC, and our proprietary field pictures. The results confirm that the proposed edge-enabled YOLOv9 framework offers an efficient, scalable, and low-latency solution for intelligent parking management systems, facilitating AI-driven smart city infrastructure to enhance mobility, safety, and environmental sustainability. © 2026 IEEE.},
