	doi = {10.1109/EEEAC71377.2026.11709444},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105054917113?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Lithium-ion battery remaining useful life (RUL) prediction is critical for reliable battery management system (BMS) operation and safety early warning. Existing deep learning-based RUL prediction models suffer from two typical engineering bottlenecks: insufficient cross-working-condition generalization ability and unbalanced contradiction between prediction accuracy and edge deployment overhead. Aiming at the above problems, this conference research proposes a systematic generalization verification and lightweight optimization framework for the spatiotemporal attention CNN-LSTM hybrid model. First, a unified battery dataset preprocessing pipeline and multi-dimensional evaluation metric system are constructed to eliminate experimental randomness. Second, the performance iteration rules of multi-scale feature extraction, residual enhancement, and spatiotemporal joint attention modules are quantitatively analyzed. Third, a lightweight pruning and adaptive scaling strategy is embedded into the established hybrid model to reduce inference latency and parameter redundancy while maintaining prediction precision. Comprehensive benchmark experiments on NASA and CALCE datasets verify that the optimized model achieves excellent balance of accuracy, generalization, and computational efficiency. Compared with baseline models, the proposed method reduces cross-dataset prediction error and realizes lightweight edge deployment. This research provides an effective engineering feasible solution for high-reliability and low-cost battery health prognosis under complex variable working conditions.  © 2026 IEEE.},
	type = {Conference paper},
