	abstract = {AbstractExisting helmet detection methods are challenged by small object detection, scene complexity, real-time inference requirements, and resource-constrained deployment. To address these issues, a lightweight real-time detection framework, termed MFG-DETR, is presented for construction helmet monitoring. The framework is built upon RT-DETR, into which three specialized components are integrated. First, a Multi-scale Lightweight Edge Detector (MLE) is introduced to improve the detection of small and distant helmets. Second, a Synergistic Dual-Stage Attention Fusion (SDSA-Fusion) module is designed to enhance feature fusion under occlusion and background clutter. Third, a Synergistic Gated Residual gConvC3 (SGR-gConvC3) module is employed to suppress background noise while maintaining computational efficiency. Experiments on three benchmark datasets (GDUT-HWD + AIGC-HWD, SHWD, and SHEL5K) show that the proposed framework achieves state-of-the-art detection accuracy with real-time inference performance and a compact model size. Edge deployment simulations further verify MFG-DETR's robustness and efficiency, confirming its practical potential for intelligent safety monitoring systems. © 2026 Elsevier B.V. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.},
