	abstract = {AI-integrated smart campuses are redefining institutional efficiency by unifying real-time attendance automation, intelligent security monitoring, and student support services through advanced edge vision and natural language processing (NLP) systems. This paper presents a comprehensive AIdriven smart campus framework designed to enhance academic operations, safety, and student-faculty interaction. The proposed system leverages lightweight CNN and Vision Transformer models deployed on edge devices for facebased attendance and real- time surveillance analytics, achieving 96.8% detection accuracy with sub- 4 5 ms inference latency. A multimodal NLP-powered student support chatbot, trained using retrieval-augmented responses, demonstrates 9 2. 4 % intent classification accuracy and reduces query resolution time by 6 1 %. Real-world deployment results show improvements in attendance efficiency (+38%), incident detection responsiveness (+47%), and faculty workload reduction (+29 %) compared to traditional systems. While the framework delivers strong gains in accuracy, speed, and autonomy, challenges remain in large-scale edge deployment, model generalization across illumination conditions, and integration with legacy campus management platforms. Future work will focus on expanding sensor fusion for environmental monitoring, developing campus- wide digital twins, and implementing privacy-preserving federated learning for secure AI-driven campus governance. © 2026 IEEE.},
