	abstract = {We present CardioGenie, a privacy-preserving sensing-to-semantics, conversational edge AI system that converts wearable ECG into real-time, clinician-in-the-loop cardiology guidance. CardioGenie continuously acquires single-lead ECG from a Polar H10 chest strap, performs artifact-robust preprocessing and feature extraction, and fuses ECG biomarkers with symptoms, laboratory results, imaging findings, and family history to construct a structured patient context. This multimodal context conditions a 7B medical small language model, MSLM (BioMistral-7B) through a clinician-curated schema, enabling generation of personalized lifestyle, medication, and diagnostic suggestions. To ensure safety under open-ended generation, CardioGenie adds a knowledge-base validation gate that checks dosage constraints, contraindications, and evidence support; detected inconsistencies trigger targeted re-prompts, reducing hallucinations before any output is surfaced. The system is deployed for patients at home via an Android client and for providers via hospital-edge inference, enabling low-latency assistance while keeping raw signals and sensitive context local. CardioGenie demonstrates how tightly-coupled sensing, multi-modal context modeling, and edge MSLM reasoning can operationalize real-time, privacy-aware decision support for personalized cardiac care. © 2026 IEEE.},
