	abstract = {Production advanced driver assistance systems integrate perception, prediction, planning, and control under strict real-time and safety constraints. This paper uses deployment artifacts from a production ADAS stack to abstract a safety-oriented reference architecture. We built a lightweight static-analysis pipeline over directory structure, deployment descriptors, configuration files, and deployed inference assets. The extracted evidence includes 7 top-level subsystem directories, 27 perception and planning-control module directories, 31 TensorRT models in 13 categories totaling 1.01 GB, service strings, and timing and fault-monitoring configurations. From these artifacts, we derive four recurring properties: modular multi-sensor perception, staged planning-control integration, explicit actuation interfaces, and a cross-layer safety support plane. The result is a bounded architecture-level abstraction for production driver-assistance systems. © 2026 IEEE.},
