	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/ISOIRS70157.2026.11545245},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105042441030?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Action generation bridges multimodal perception and physical control in embodied agents. Existing attention-based vision-language-action (VLA) action experts can achieve strong accuracy, but their token-level cross-attention is computationally expensive and less suitable for long-horizon, on-device deployment. We propose to model action generation as a state-space process and introduce Cross-SSM (Cross-conditioned State-Space Model), a cache-free, linear-time action expert. Cross-SSM replaces transformer cross-attention with linear context aggregation and recurrent state updates while preserving the surrounding VLA architecture and training pipeline. The latent action state recursively integrates visual, language, and proprioceptive context, enabling predictable memory usage and temporally coherent control. Experiments on Meta-World, LIBERO, and RoboTwin show competitive or improved success rates, lower per-step inference latency, and smoother long-horizon trajectories. © 2026 IEEE.},
