	abstract = {Underground coal mining remains a backbone of the global and specifically Indian energy infrastructure but poses serious health and explosion risks from dust and toxic gases. Traditional monitoring relies on sparse, manual sampling. New systems based on the Internet of Things (IoT) rely heavily on cloud processing, introducing dangerous detection delays due to connectivity issues. This work presents an end-to-end system that combines distributed IoT sensing, on-site Edge Artificial Intelligence (AI), generative data synthesis, and a digital twin to realize real-time, high-resolution Air Quality Index (AQI) monitoring. This system mitigates latency issues by processing data in the Edge, so that alerts are available despite connectivity issues. The system presented in this paper is an end-to-end IoT system that includes Custom End Devices that are connected via a wired network to a powerful Jetson Orin based Edge Device. The paper also presents a combination of data preprocessing, feature extraction, and feature selection, integarted with an ensemble Machine Learning Algorithm that has been customized for Mine Monitoring Applications. Lab based test under simulated mine conditions confirm sub-second hazard detection with an accuracy higher than 97%, validating the system's effectiveness for low-latency, edge-based mine safety monitoring. © 2026 The Authors.},
