	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105022843493?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Ensuring the operational reliability of high-voltage power transmission corridors necessitates continuous and efficient monitoring solutions. This paper presents the lightweight edge AI (L-EAI) framework, a modular edge architecture optimized for anomaly detection under constrained embedded conditions. The framework integrates commercial-grade network cameras with NVIDIA Jetson Nano edge devices, employing adaptive frame sampling to balance energy efficiency and detection accuracy. A three-phase model optimization strategy is proposed. It comprises knowledge distillation, structured pruning, and post-training quantization, which together enable the deployment of compact and robust deep learning models. Experimental deployments across 28 monitoring stations in Vietnam demonstrate that the L-EAI framework achieves competitive detection accuracy while significantly reducing inference latency and power consumption compared to baseline approaches. By incorporating region-of-interest processing and human-in-the-loop validation, the system continuously adapts to environmental variability and operational challenges. The L-EAI framework highlights the potential for reusable and generalizable embedded software architectures in critical infrastructure monitoring. © 2025 Elsevier B.V.},
