	abstract = {The high rate of development of the independent UAV systems requires powerful and smart perception units to provide safe and effective navigation. In this paper, we present a real-time solution for zero-shot detection of specific drone landing zones based on Grounding DINO and YOLOv12 with a transformer-based vision-language model. Our model utilizes the speed of object localization of YOLOv12 and adds a transformer head to it to match visual representations with textual representations, which allows zero-shot generalization to previously unseen landing zones. In order to make the trained model practically deployable, it is packaged into a Flask-based web application that offers a RESTful API to make real-time inferences using aerial images or video feeds. This enables easy integration with UAV systems to be deployed onboard or on the edge. The model was tested on a custom set with different helipad designs, backgrounds and lighting conditions. To measure the accuracy of detection and the generalization, evaluation measures are Mean Average Precision, Precision, Recall, and F1-score. The study shows that it is possible to implement zero-shot drone landing zone recognition practice into the field environment, which does not require exhaustive retraining and provides a versatile solution to autonomous drone tasks in new and unobservable settings. © 2026 IEEE.},
