	abstract = {There is a growing elderly population living alone or who are left momentarily unsupervised when their caretaker or family members are out working. There is a demand for innovative assistive technologies that enable independent living while maintaining quality of life. This paper presents Homeyx, a distributed Physical AI-based multimodal assistive robot designed for elderly home environments. A Raspberry Pi 5 is combined with a cognitive layer using a locally installed LLaMA 3 language model, deterministic motion control using ESP32, vision-based perception, and the Sarvam AI platform for multilingual conversation. A rule-based, safety-constrained medical advisory module with Indic language support is also incorporated. The system operates fully on-device for essential tasks, removing reliance on cloud dependency for sensitive medical interactions and ensuring user data privacy. Groq-Accelerated Whisper is employed for low-latency speech recognition. Experimental results demonstrate 95 % vision accuracy, sub-second end-To-end response times (avg. 825 ms), over 91 % multilingual recognition accuracy across English, Hindi, and Malayalam, and 92.6 % advisory precision, at a total hardware cost of approximately Rs. 18,000.  © 2026 IEEE.},
