	abstract = {To address the challenges of balancing real-time performance and detection accuracy in operation and maintenance safety monitoring, and the insufficient adaptability of existing algorithms to edge devices, a lightweight attentionenhanced YOLO-Fast Edge algorithm is proposed to construct a real-time monitoring model for operation and maintenance safety based on edge machine vision. This algorithm utilizes depth wise separable convolution combined with channel pruning to construct a lightweight backbone network. It innovatively introduces a spatial-channel dual-dimensional attention enhancement mechanism to improve small target detection capabilities and employs an improved non-maximum suppression algorithm to optimize post-processing efficiency. The constructed model encompasses four main modules: edge image acquisition and preprocessing, target detection, real-time decision-making and early warning, and edge-cloud data synchronization and traceability. Tensors quantization is used for deployment and adaptation to edge devices. Experimental results show that the YOLO-Fast Edge algorithm achieves an mAP@ 0.5 of 89.7%, with an FPS of 28.3 on a Jetson Nano device and only 2.1M parameters. Compared with mainstream lightweight algorithms such as YOLOv5s and YOLOv7-tiny, it has significant advantages in detection accuracy, real-time performance, and lightweight design. It can run stably on edge devices with different computing power, such as Raspberry Pi 4B and Atlas 200 DK, and exhibits good robustness in scenarios with strong light, occlusion, and complex backgrounds. This model enables high-precision, low-latency monitoring of personnel violations, equipment malfunctions, and hazardous targets in operation and maintenance scenarios, providing technical support for the application of edge machine vision in the field of operation and maintenance safety. © 2026 IEEE.},
