	abstract = {Screening for retinal disease is essential to prevent irreversible vision loss, but traditional screening methods rely on costly stationary imaging systems and trained expertise. These have limited access in areas that are distant or resource-poor. More than that, when do a screening manually, it relies on human expertise that can be variable in accuracy, reliability, consistency and turnaround time. Here, introduces an Edge AI-Based Portable Retina Disease Screening Device – an intelligent autonomous system, that automates high-definition fundus imaging and real-time classification of various diseases directly on a portable device, such as NVIDIA Jetson or Raspberry Pi. Without this system, retinal disease detection relies on imaging and then offline processing of those images by specialist(s) to interpret significance and/or clinical treatment, which can add delays that influence time to clinical intervention. This integrated system acts like a stand-alone imagine and diagnosis device, utilizing convolutional neural networks (CNNs) with task-based models optimized for edge deployment, storing testing images locally and reporting outcomes all free of any external cloud connections. Studies have demonstrated that the proposed device maintains high classification accuracy with low latency, while also maintaining low power consumption, and provides substantial innovations in accessibility and response time when compared to existing tele-ophthalmology approaches and provides a clear marking towards democratizing AI-powered eye screening, enabling early detection and intervention at the point of care, especially in underserved communities. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.},
