	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105042312829?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {We present an AI-powered navigation pipeline that detects road hazards - including potholes, lane violations, and accident scenarios - in near real time using lightweight deep-learning detectors (YOLOv8 variants), a CNN-based road-surface classification module, and OpenCV-driven lane geometry extraction. The system processes continuous video streams from dashcams or mobile devices, performs multi-hazard inference, and generates instant audio/visual alerts to warn drivers of critical on-road events. A hazard-aware rerouting module further enhances safety by dynamically adjusting the navigation path based on detected anomalies. The proposed model is trained and evaluated using a hybrid dataset composed of RDD2020 pothole samples, KITTI lane images, diverse YouTube Road footage, and custom data captured from Indian roads to ensure robustness under varying lighting, weather, and traffic conditions. Experimental analysis demonstrates strong performance across tasks, with notable improvements in detection accuracy, reduced false positives, and stable real-time inference following edge-focused optimizations such as model quantization, pruning, and selective frame sampling. Overall, the system transforms traditional navigation solutions into intelligent driver-assistance platforms capable of proactive hazard detection, real-time road-condition monitoring, and enhanced situational awareness for safer transportation. © 2026 IEEE.},
