	abstract = {The rapid growth of the aging population has intensified the need for intelligent systems that ensure safety, independence, and timely healthcare support for elderly individuals. This paper presents an integrated framework for activity recognition and assisted monitoring in elderly homes using Edge-AI. The proposed system combines real-time pose estimation, machine learning based activity classification, and IoT-enabled alert mechanisms deployed on a compact edge server. The edge server performs on-device inference using an optimized XGBoost classifier to distinguish normal daily activities from potential fall events. Skeletal key points are extracted using MediaPipe Pose and processed for robust activity recognition. Upon detecting a fall, the system triggers immediate alert notifications to remote caregivers for timely intervention. By operating entirely on edge infrastructure, the proposed system achieves low-latency response, enhanced data privacy, and reduced reliance on cloud connectivity. A lightweight dashboard interface further enables visualization of activity logs for long-term behavioral monitoring and trend analysis. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed Edge-AI framework offers a cost-effective, responsive, and scalable solution for intelligent elderly care in resourceconstrained environments.  © 2026 IEEE.},
