	abstract = {Autonomous collection of student feedback during counselling hours requires a private-by-design, conversational, and sensitive-escalation feedback system. In this review, we present a Vision-Speech enabled feedback systems embedded in feedback in humanoid agents framed in a Jetson based deployment of EduBot Insight (Fig. 1–2). We reviewed 27 peer reviewed papers (2020–2024) in IEEE Xplore, Scopus, and ACM DL using the query (feedback OR counselling) AND (humanoid OR conversational agent) AND (privacy OR anonymity) and coded each papers based on sensing modality, speech stack, anonymisation method, safety detection, and interaction design. Three key contributions come out of these observations: (1) edge deployed 4-bit instruction-tuned LLMs enable fast grounded dialogue on a 10 W budget; (2) on-device ASR (such as Vosk) with low-latency streaming maintains natural flow in Indian English accents; (3) anonymous-mode agents with class-level aggregation improves student disclosure rates and mitigates social inhibition in feedback sessions. In conclusion, we present future challenges in affective bias, threshold calibration for safety alerts, and responsible audit logging to provide a road-map to an empathetic, privacy-preserving classroom agent. ©2026 IEEE.},
