	abstract = {Human-wildlife conflict in a g ricultural re gions results in significant c r op d a mage, p a rticularly i n re mote areas lacking stable infrastructure. This work presents an edge AIbased wildlife classification a ndde terrence prototype designed for low-power, offline d eployment. A M obileNetV2 convolutional neural network (CNN) is trained to classify nine wildlife species associated with farm intrusion and optimized using full-integer INT8 quantization for efficient e m bedded i n ference. T h eoptimized model is deployed on the PYNQ-Z2 platform based on the Xilinx Zynq-7000 SoC, performing on-device inference using TensorFlow Lite on the ARM Cortex-A9 processor without cloud dependency. Experimental validation demonstrates high classification a c curacy wi th a compact model si ze of 2.74 MB achieving an average inference latency of approximately 680 ms per frame and an estimated power consumption of approximately 2.5 W. A species-specific d eterrence c ontrol l ayer is implemented in the Programmable Logic (PL) using a custom Register Transfer Level (RTL) based finite s tate m achine, i ntegrated with the Processing System (PS) via the AXI-Lite interface, enabling deterministic low-latency GPIO actuation independent of Linux software scheduling delays. The post-implementation analysis demonstrates that the hardware controller occupies only 1.09% LUT utilization on the Zynq-7020 programmable logic fabric. The results demonstrate the feasibility of deploying lightweight wildlife classification s ystems on r esource-constrained embedded platforms for autonomous agricultural monitoring applications. © 2026 IEEE.},
