	abstract = {A real-time, context-aware system that can concurrently monitor driver behavior and identify dynamic road barriers is necessary to ensure road safety. This research presents a novel hybrid framework that combines EfficientNet-B2 improved with Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) attention for distraction classification with YOLOv7-tiny for obstacle detection. By combining cross-domain data from both driver and road perspectives, the system is further enhanced by Hierarchical Attention Distillation (HAD) and Gradient-Sensitive Spatial Encoding (GSSE). The Hybrid Firefly - Whale Optimization Algorithm (HFWOA) is used for optimization in order to balance low-latency performance and detection accuracy on embedded devices such as Jetson Xavier NX. In real-time at geqslant 3 0 frames per second, evaluation results demonstrate an accuracy of 94.6% for distraction classification, mean average precision (mAP) of 0.99, and IoU up to 0.97 in road obstacle recognition. Adaptive fusion across views based on scene criticality is ensured by the Contextual Voting Attention (CVA) module. A high-fidelity perception model appropriate for incorporation into autonomous or ADAS systems is offered by this dual-stream ensemble framework. The suggested approach lowers the likelihood of accidents brought on by distraction or missing driving indications by concurrently analyzing driver states and external threats. © 2026 IEEE.},
