	doi = {10.1109/HYDCON48903.2020.9242815},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85096864331?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {The nervous system of the digital society will be based on 5G. It will have new services based on devices, machines. Smart things and robots will use the apps, services and the data using the 5G network. Cognition as a service (CAAS) will be the kernel of the 5G network spanning the devices and terminals. CaaS will load first and stay in memory. All the important services are initialized and it will manage the devices and the resources in the 5G hardware. CaaS will help in creating the new ecosystems which are based on the low reaction times. For example, autonomous cars, robot as a services and self-acting machines require very low reaction time.Cognitive capabilities are provided by CaaS and the applications are easily developed based on the APIs. The capabilities are based on techniques such as nonlinear systems, adaptive control, fuzzy systems, and artificial intelligence. Data is gathered from the sensors, terminals, things, and machines. The fixed and mobile low latency networks exchange and transfer the data. CaaS acts as the nervous system to collate, elaborate and exchange the information. CaaS helps in understanding the environment and provides the capability to adapt to changes. The reaction times for adaptation need to be appropriate based on the scenario. This is because the 5G network will have latency in the order of milliseconds. Edge cognition will have low latency in the order of 1 to 5 ms. Centralized cognition will have in the range of 20 to 30 ms. Edge cognition will be near the devices, robots, cars, and machines. Centralized cognition will be for the systems on the cloud.  © 2020 IEEE.},
