	abstract = {A 0.4M parameter ultra-lightweight pose estimation network design based on an edge convolutional neural network (CNN) accelerator is presented. The design aims at achieving efficient and real-time edge deployment of human pose estimation, which is essential in cutting-edge fields such as human-robot interaction. The proposed pose estimation network utilizes parallelized feature pyramid network and customized ConvMixer to enable the feature extraction network to have larger and more discrete backpropagation gradients. In addition, an efficient accelerator with an overlap pattern architecture was designed for the network, and FPGA prototype validation achieved real-time inference at 21.5 frames per second (FPS). © 2025 IEEE.},
