	doi = {10.1109/ICRAS70064.2026.11717994},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105055218065?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Semantic segmentation is a key component of autonomous delivery robots operating under strict onboard computational constraints. In this work, we redesign EfficientDet for real-Time segmentation and propose a deployment-oriented scaling strategy that decouples BiFPN and segmentation head capacities. Experiments on the AIHub Surface Masking dataset and Jetson Orin Nano show that segmentation performance does not increase monotonically with model complexity, and lightweight prediction heads are critical for stable runtime stability. The selected configuration with BiFPN width 96 and depth 2 and segmentation head width 32 and depth 2 improves mIoU by 3.76% over the baseline, increases throughput by 7.88 FPS, and reduces P99 latency by 0.82 ms. These results demonstrate that deployment-Aware scaling can simultaneously enhance accuracy and worst-case runtime behavior, making the proposed model suitable for embedded robotic deployment.  © 2026 IEEE.},
