	abstract = {Detecting potential damage to unattended vehicles is crucial in urban environments where vandalism and harm are common. This paper introduces a low-power, real-time threat detection system combining ultrasonic sensors and artificial intelligence (AI) powered red, green, and blue (RGB) cameras. The system uses an NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano and STM32 microcontroller for efficient operation. Ultrasonic sensors activate the Jetson platform upon detecting threats, triggering object detection, pose estimation and action recognition algorithms. A live video feed is streamed via the web real-time communication (WebRTC) protocol for high-quality, low-latency remote monitoring and alerts. This paper intends to demonstrate how a modular architecture can integrate multi-modal sensor data acquisition and recognition for incident logging while implementing power optimization techniques that ensure energy-efficient operation suitable for prolonged use, making them ideal for operation even during the vacation mode of electric vehicles (EVs) [1]. This research highlights the significance of real-time monitoring and demonstrates the potential of AI-powered embedded systems that enhance parking safety. It also proposes future enhancements to optimize detection capabilities further and provide a foundation for future enhancements, such as autonomous response systems.  © 2025 IEEE.},
