	abstract = {Fashion recommendations often rely on fragmented cloud-based systems that compromise user privacy. We present an end-to-end, on-device fashion assistant combining Korean seasonal color analysis with body shape classification to generate holistic styling guidance. Our system fine-tunes DinoV2 vision transformers achieving 61% seasonal accuracy and employs Qwen3-7B vision-language models achieving 58% body shape accuracy on a new curated celebrity dataset (1,482 images, 4 body types). A rule-based engine integrates color theory with silhouette recommendations, uniquely providing both positive suggestions and negative guidance ("what to avoid"). The system runs entirely on-device with 5-second end-to-end latency on 8GB RAM smartphones, eliminating cloud dependency while delivering 20-25 personalized recommendations per session. Our contributions include a novel body shape dataset, a hybrid vision transformer and vision-language model approach, and complete local processing for privacy-preserving fashion recommendations. © 2025 IEEE.},
