	abstract = {The growing demand for real-time and intelligent inspection in data centers and industrial facilities highlights the limitations of mobile robots constrained by onboard computing resources. To address this challenge, an edge-robot collaborative inspection framework is proposed, integrating an indoor edge-cloud base station with a mobile inspection robot via a 5G network. By offloading visual inference tasks to a nearby edge server, the system achieves real-time object detection with low communication latency. Experimental results show that the end- to-end delay is maintained at around 14 ms while sustaining over 30 FPS detection performance, confirming the feasibility of low-latency edge inference for indoor inspection scenarios. © 2025 IEEE.},
