	abstract = {The rapid growth of urban populations has intensified traffic congestion, making real-time monitoring and predictive management essential for smart city infrastructure. This paper proposes a deep learning-driven Edge-AI framework deployed on autonomous unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) to perform real-time traffic analysis, incident detection, and congestion prediction in dynamic urban environments. The system integrates high-resolution aerial video capture with on-board deep convolutional neural networks (CNNs) and transformer-based architectures optimized for edge inference, eliminating reliance on constant cloud connectivity. A multi-stage processing pipeline enables vehicle detection, trajectory extraction, and traffic flow estimation directly on the UAV, followed by edge-to-edge coordination between drones for large-scale coverage. Experiments conducted on publicly available drone-traffic datasets, enhanced with custom aerial recordings, demonstrate that the proposed approach achieves over 94% detection accuracy with sub second inference latency, while significantly reducing bandwidth usage compared to cloud-based methods. The framework's adaptability to varying traffic densities and lighting conditions highlights its potential for deployment in Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS), urban planning, and emergency response. This work contributes a scalable, privacy-preserving, and latency-optimized solution for next-generation traffic management in smart cities.  © 2025 IEEE.},
